{
  "info": {
    "name": "Seat Ase? API",
    "description": "Every endpoint of the Seat Ase? API, in story order: Jashim goes online, Nusrat and Rafiq book, Jashim pools them into Bullet, drives, and drops them off (Scenario A).\n\nRun it: `docker compose up`, import this file, then run the whole collection with the Collection Runner (or `npx newman run postman/seat-ase.postman_collection.json`). It needs a freshly seeded cast with no active bookings.\n\nLogin is an httpOnly cookie. Postman keeps one cookie per host, so each folder starts by logging in as whoever acts in it. Every seeded account uses the password `password123`.\n\nLive updates (GET /events/stream) are not in the run: an SSE stream never ends, so a runner would wait on it forever. Watch it with curl instead: log in with `curl -c nusrat.txt -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"phone\":\"01700000030\",\"password\":\"password123\"}' http://localhost:4000/auth/login`, then `curl -N -b nusrat.txt http://localhost:4000/events/stream`. It sends {\"type\":\"heartbeat\"} every 25s and nudges like {\"type\":\"ride.updated\",\"action\":\"REQUEST_MATCHED\",\"rideId\":\"...\"}. Nudges never carry data; the screen refetches through the normal API.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000"
    },
    {
      "key": "bananiZoneId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "mohakhaliZoneId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "nusratRequestId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "rafiqRequestId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "rideId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
